executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Under the protected profile, an IDE passes --protected-project <project> to the daemon's accounts CLI. Every command that runs claude then resolves claude only in absolute PATH entries whose real path, and every ancestor of it, is not the project, or in an absolute MOE_CLAUDE_BIN outside the project. The claude child then runs with:
- PATH = exactly those entries, as real paths, in order;
- cwd = the home folder, outside the project;
- on Windows, NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath=1, and for a .cmd/.bat claude the absolute %SystemRoot%/System32/cmd.exe as its shell.
So neither claude, nor the node an npm shim starts, nor the project's .claude settings is reached through the project cwd or through an empty, '.', relative or in-project PATH entry. When that is impossible, the CLI exits 1 with MOE_PROTECTED_CLAUDE_NOT_FOUND or MOE_PROTECTED_CLAUDE_REFUSED, before any folder, prompt, registry write or spawn.
Both IDEs pass the option on every protected Accounts line:
- JetBrains on its protected PowerShell, bash and WSL routes;
- VS Code on win32 and POSIX, typed and clipboard lines alike, with the workspace folder protectedAccountsTerminal checked (AccountsTerminal.project).
Without the option, the CLI and every legacy Accounts line in either IDE behave exactly as before. The docs for the contract follow in task-3a98393f.
